  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan Flood Response and Recovery 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since mid-June 2022, up to 33 million people in Pakistan have been affected by severe monsoon weather, causing flash floods and landslides, which have resulted in severe loss of human lives, property, and infrastructure as well as the displacement of 7.9 million people. The flooding significantly damaged infrastructure, destroying 2.9 million homes and displacing a considerable part of the population. More than one million people still live near flood waters, as of May 2023, and over 4.5 million people do not have access to safe drinking water due to destroyed or contaminated water sources. In continuation of its floods response, IOM is enhancing coordination efforts for the emergency Shelter and Non-food Items (S/NFI) sector in Pakistan and mobilizing Pakistani diaspora in the United Kingdom to better understand its current and future engagement with flood affected people in Pakistan. This includes the reinforcement of streamlined coordination in the Emergency S/NFI and the Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) sector coordination mechanisms, and mapping of Pakistani diaspora in the United Kingdom of Great Britain and their involvement to humanitarian responses to the flood affected people in Pakistan.</narrative>
  </description>
